Package: rdz
Title: Fast Serialization of R Objects
Version: 0.0.1
Authors@R: c(
    person("Pedro", "Baltazar", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           email = "pedrobtz@gmail.com"),
    person("Yann", "Collet", role = "cph",
           comment = "Author of the bundled LZ4 library"))
Description: Provides a native serialization path for common R
    vectors, lists, matrices, and data frames. String vectors adapt between
    dictionary and flat layouts. An optional balanced preset dictionary-encodes
    low-cardinality numeric vectors with bit-packed and optionally 'LZ4'-compressed
    indexes, packs logical vectors into two bits per value, packs small-range
    integer offsets, and stores exact constant-delta numeric sequences
    compactly. High-cardinality doubles can use an exact XOR-delta and
    byte-transpose transform with independent 'LZ4' blocks when it saves at least
    12.5 percent. Flat string payloads use independent 'LZ4' blocks and run-length
    encoded metadata only when the combined representation is smaller.
    Unsupported objects automatically fall back to R's general serialization
    format.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Depends:
    R (>= 4.1.0)
Encoding: UTF-8
RoxygenNote: 8.0.0
Suggests:
    data.table,
    testthat (>= 3.0.0),
